    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="0590" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/893: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-10T11:00:00+08:00">November 10,
                            1941—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:59 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>343. The American community at Peiping has reacted favorably to the President’s
                    remarks that consideration is being given to the withdrawal of the Marines from
                    Peiping, reasoning that they would be ineffective because of smallness of
                    numbers in any military engagement and that it would be a shame to incur any
                    serious risk of their internment.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking, Tientsin, Shanghai and Manila for
                    Commander-in-Chief Asiatic Fleet.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butrick</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
